From a54a522dbd2112da48a1b5416681508cc2561dca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: W1nkelm4nn <mrmarkap61@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 23:09:29 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] dxvk: Support portability devices such as MoltenVK.

MoltenVK lacks geometryShader, shaderCullDistance, depthClipEnable,
robustBufferAccess2 and nullDescriptor, so the device was rejected.
On portability devices (VK_KHR_portability_subset, or the MoltenVK
driver ID since Wine does not expose that extension to Windows
applications) these features are now optional:

- geometry shaders and cull distances only fail for shaders using them
- depth clip is approximated with depth clamp, like DXVK 1.x did
- null descriptors are replaced with zero-initialized dummy resources
  (DxvkNullResources), created per context on first use and
  initialized through the init command buffer

Other devices keep the strict requirements.
